# `power::OutageResult`

Flows after every single-line outage.

## Signature

```cpp
power::OutageResult
```

## What It Does

The result of `outages`.

## Fields

| Field | Meaning | Default |
|---|---|---|
| `base_flow` | The DC flows before any outage, `[..., line]`. |  |
| `flow` | The flows after each outage, `[..., outage line, monitored line]`; the row of an invalid outage is `NaN`. |  |
| `valid` | True for each outage that is a valid single-line contingency, `[..., outage line]`. |  |

## Returns

Returned by `outages`.

## Errors

Reading a field does not compute again.

## Interpretation and Use

Compare `flow` with the line ratings in one array operation, and read `valid` with it: a comparison with `NaN` is false and would pass an invalid outage as safe.

